zizhan: keep two empty pooled blocks per pool instead of one (backboardd re-made and mapped a 64 MiB block at every
home-screen animation; docs/progress/2026-11-01-120hz-and-cadence.md section 8).

--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/memory.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/memory.rs
@@ -51,6 +51,13 @@
 /// The size of a pooled block, at most the device's `maxMemoryAllocationSize`.
 pub(super) const BLOCK_BYTES: u64 = 64 << 20;
 
+/// The empty pooled blocks a pool keeps (zizhan, docs/progress/2026-11-01-120hz-and-cadence.md section 8). With one, every
+/// home-screen animation paid 150-200 ms in backboardd's display thread: Core Animation's new surface filled the kept block past
+/// half, [`keep_room`] made a 64 MiB block (allocated, zeroed, write-combined and mapped page by page, 16384 pages), and when the
+/// surface went both blocks were empty and one was freed again. Two keep the pair across animations; memory pressure still trims
+/// them ([`Memory::trim_empty_blocks`]).
+pub(super) const KEPT_EMPTY_BLOCKS: usize = 2;
+
 /// What memory a resource needs.
 #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
 pub(super) enum MemoryClass {
